# The kpp version's text files are LF in every checkout: the pages' HTML is in raw string literals,
# which kpp (unlike C++ compilers) keeps a CRLF checkout's CR in, so a FreeBSD program built on
# CI's Windows runner (core.autocrlf true) wrote its pages with CRLF (run 41867124956); and the
# expected pages in testdata/ are compared byte for byte.
* text=auto eol=lf
